From 5d534bacbb6327e09aedf95c55ddcacf4b8f9455 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:17:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 59/59] ntdll: MetalSharp Wine's graphics lanes on x86_64:
 VKD3D / DXVK, WineMetalGL, and DLSS on every lane.

Wine loads each lane by itself from GRAPHICS_BACKEND (a game's .metalsharp/launch.env), as MetalSharp Wine does:

- VKD3D / DXVK (GRAPHICS_BACKEND vkd3d, dxvk; vulkan and vkd3d-proton from older routes): VKD3D-Proton's
  d3d12/d3d12core with DXVK's dxgi/d3d11/d3d10core, the lane's own NGX core and NVAPI, and DXVK's d3d9/d3d8 and
  32-bit DLLs, from ~/.metalsharp/vkd3d or MetalSharp-Wine-x86_64.app's share/metalsharp/vkd3d. Their WINEDLLPATH
  comes first; entries inside Wine's own dll_dir are skipped there, since a builtin found as a flat WINEDLLPATH
  entry looks for its Unix library beside it (crypt32 and win32u failed to start, c0000142, in games the Steam
  client started: its wrapper puts lib/wine/<arch>-windows in WINEDLLPATH).
- The DLL path is set again once launch.env is applied, for the lane the program chose rather than the one of the
  program that started it.
- WineMetalGL is the default OpenGL when it's bundled (lib/winemetalgl; OPENGL_BACKEND=wine or WINEMETALGL=0 for
  Wine's own).
- Default DXMT_RUNTIME_DIR, D3DMETAL_RUNTIME_DIR and WFDXCOMPAT_RUNTIME_DIR next to Wine.
- A 32-bit program on the VKD3D / DXVK lane starts without MTL_HUD_ENABLED: the Metal HUD throws an Objective-C
  exception (nil dictionary key) in a 32-bit MoltenVK device (Portal 2 on DXVK's D3D9).
- DLSS: games that come with it are set up on Mullion, VKD3D / DXVK and D3DMetal. DXVK's DXGI gets the NVIDIA
  identity through DXVK_CONFIG; D3DMetal through D3DM_VENDOR_ID, D3DM_DEVICE_ID and D3DM_DEVICE_DESCRIPTION (it
  reports "AMD Compatibility Mode" otherwise). D3DMetal's nvngx.dll is nvngx-on-metalfx.dll, and now its Unix
  library is nvngx-on-metalfx.so too: before, its DllMain failed (ERROR_DLL_INIT_FAILED).
- MetalFX scale settings are read from vkd3d.conf and dxvk.conf on the VKD3D / DXVK lane.
- launch.env: the image path is read from its place after curdir and dllpath in the startup info.
